<h2>A checklist before you buy</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Confirm the event name, date, time and venue.</li>
  <li>Check the section, row and number of seats.</li>
  <li>Read the delivery method so you know how tickets will reach you.</li>
  <li>Review the full cost at checkout.</li>
  <li>Save your confirmation email and order number.</li>
</ol>
<p>The Federal Trade Commission has <a href="https://consumer.ftc.gov/articles/how-avoid-scam" target="_blank" rel="noopener">straightforward advice on how to avoid a scam</a>, and our own guide covers <a href="/blog/how-to-avoid-ticket-scams">ticket scams</a> in detail.</p>

<h2>If something goes wrong</h2>
<p>Act quickly and keep records. Contact <a href="/ticket-customer-service">customer service</a> with your order number and details, ideally well before the event. You can also email <a href="mailto:support@seatoutlet.com">support@seatoutlet.com</a>. We cannot give a fixed number of days for a refund, because timing depends on the payment provider and the event.</p>
<p>Many questions are answered in the <a href="/ticket-faq">ticket FAQ</a>. For the legal wording, see our <a href="/terms-and-conditions">terms and conditions</a>.</p>

